{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["And the reason for <b>אֶת ה׳ הֶאֱמַרְתָּ הַיּוֹם</b> (\"You have declared HaShem this day\"): since you have accepted upon yourselves the entire Torah — its explanations, its precise rules, and its novellae — behold, you have exalted HaShem and lifted Him up, that He alone shall be your Elohim; you shall not acknowledge any other el at all." "<b>וְלָלֶכֶת בִּדְרָכָיו</b> (\"and to walk in His ways\"), that you should do the good and the upright and bestow kindness, each man upon his fellow; and <b>to keep His statutes and His commandments and His ordinances</b> — He specifies the statutes and the ordinances in particular, as I have explained (Ramban on Deuteronomy 4:5), and He includes in <b>His commandments</b> all the commandments, positive and negative, and <b>to obey His voice</b>, according to all that He may command you of the remaining matters, whether through me or through the rest of the prophets, as I have explained (Ramban on Deuteronomy 13:5). And it is possible that <b>His commandments</b> refers to positive commandments and <b>to obey His voice</b> refers to the prohibitions, that is to say, negative commandments."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:56:02.548169145Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}